course: dictionary
lesson: 14773
title: Words that stick out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word protruding means sticking out from a surface or an edge. Something that is protruding pokes out past the rest of the thing it is attached to.
explain: «A nail was protruding from the wall, so Mia hung her coat on a hook instead.» The nail sticks out, and a coat could get torn on it. The clue is in the sentence: Mia chose a hook because the nail was a problem.
explain: Protruding comes from the verb protrude, which means to stick out. «The branch protrudes over the path» tells you the branch reaches out past the edge of the path. Check your meaning by swapping it in: sticking out still makes sense.
fact: Protruding means sticking out from a surface or edge.
fact: «Protruding» is a form of the verb «protrude», which means to stick out.
fact: «Protruding teeth» means teeth that stick out beyond the others.
fact: «Protruding rocks» are rocks that stick out and can trip you up or cut you.
fact: A good check is to swap in «sticking out» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «A nail was protruding from the wall.» What does protruding mean here? | Lying flat on the floor | *Sticking out from the wall | Hidden inside the wall | Painted bright red
exercise: «The rocks were protruding from the cliff, so we walked carefully.» Why did they walk carefully? | The cliff was painted | *The rocks sticking out could trip them or cut them | It was too dark to see anything | The rocks were soft and warm
exercise: «The dog's bone was protruding from the bin.» Find and copy the word that tells you the bone was sticking out. | *protruding | dog's | bin | bone
test: «Her protruding teeth were easy to see when she smiled.» What does protruding describe? | Teeth that have fallen out | *Teeth that stick out beyond the others | Teeth that hurt when she eats | Teeth that are clean and white
test: «Yesterday the sign protruded into the road.» What does the verb protrude mean? | To shine brightly | *To stick out | To fall down | To hide
exam: Mia says protruding means hidden. Which answer is correct? | Mia is right, because protruding means hidden | *Mia is wrong, because protruding means sticking out | Protruding means the same as shiny | Protruding means very cold
